WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:02.890
I'm sorry we have to drop you off here.

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.490
You're releasing me?

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:08.110
We can't just drag you around.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.930
It's yours.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.110
I can have it?

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.610
I don't care if you feel 
the need to draw it on me.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.530
Be careful now.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.650
See you around, Sayaka-chan!

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.710
So have you gotten all you 
needed from your conversation?

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.550
More or less.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.740
For now, we've decided on a place to meet.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.470
It's probably best that I don't ask, then.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.970
<b>What's this?</b>

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.970
<b>Meeting place.</b>

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.970
Just delete that app, too.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:52.980
They're probably all over my place now.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.190
They're likely also tracking this car.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:56.860
Huh?

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.730
There's a thing called the N-system—

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.860
Figures, there's the police.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.940
I'll have to let you off here.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.330
Ah, Rui-san, I'm sorry for all the trouble 
and not being able to properly thank you.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.710
Don't worry about it. Get going.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.670
We'll be going, then.

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:18.890
You've got a tough road ahead. Good luck.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:22.010
Where are we going?

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.370
Ebisu.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:51.450
<b>Katana Maidens</b>

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.240
Sunlight is the best, but...

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:11.330
<b>Episode 4  The Burden of Resolution</b>

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.870
It's still way too early in the year for this.

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.200
Take that!

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.070
Sorry!

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.070
Won't you play, too, Kaoru?

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.960
I'll pass.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:25.800
Hi!

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.760
Huh, a mission? That's sudden.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:32.010
No way. Tell them we're on vacation.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.850
"No way, we're on vacation," she says.

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.060
<i>God damn it, Kaoru, stop screwing around!</i>

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:43.790
But even if there is a mission, 
I don't have Nenekirimaru.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.470
I sent it home via express service yesterday.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.900
<i>I'm sending it back.</i>

00:03:56.570 --> 00:03:57.330
Wow.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.380
What a waste of tax dollars.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:10.840
Are you prepared to kill her, then?!

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.470
I won't kill her!

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.230
Thank you so much.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:23.500
We appreciate the help.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:31.370
I'm pretty tired.
 What about you, Hiyori-chan?

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.660
Hiyori-chan?

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:34.880
Kanami...

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.170
What is it?

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:38.770
You have helped me out considerably.

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:42.530
I am grateful, but we should part ways here.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:46.590
But I said that I would go with you.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:51.970
After this point, there is no way
 you can continue with me.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.820
Why not?

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:59.910
I realized last night that your sword 
and mine are completely different.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:03.730
My sword is one that kills,
while yours is one that protects.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.590
Only a sword that kills is needed now.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.510
Don't just decide that by yourself.

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:12.030
You just think that's the case.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:17.030
Kanami, have you ever 
actually cut down anyone?

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.330
Not their utsushi?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.610
Yes, or a human controlled by an aradama.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:27.420
I haven't.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:32.110
In recent years, there haven't been many 
cases of humans being taken over by aradama.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.290
But not too long ago,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:39.430
at least until my mother's generation,
 it wasn't so unusual.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:43.060
Humans controlled by aradama 
are no longer human.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:47.010
While they may retain their memories and 
are able to speak and answer questions,

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.150
an aradama is an aradama.

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:51.430
You get rid of them by 
killing them with okatana.

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.440
There is no other way to save them.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:58.660
We Toji are priestesses who bear the 
burden of the sins of our ancestors

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.690
and continue to appease them.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:05.450
I know that.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:09.780
What I am going to do is 
exterminate the aradama,

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.220
but it is essentially murdering someone.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:17.610
I will kill Origami Yukari and 
anyone who tries to stop me.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.070
It has come extremely 
close to being a grudge.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:26.370
But you cannot kill,
 so we will part ways here.

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:29.060
Wait!

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:32.670
You're slow.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:42.120
You should go back. Go back and 
protect people from the aradama.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.770
I'm sorry for worrying you, Shibata-san.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:56.020
Yes, please make sure my father, mother,

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.010
Miu, and Shiori won't worry, too.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:02.980
How long are you staying here, Yanase-san?

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:07.410
As long as President Hashima 
remains here. What about you?

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.310
I'm going back today.

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.310
I see.

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:17.500
I wanted to go back with Juujou-san, 
since we came here together.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:19.950
Sayaka!

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:26.170
Come with me.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:33.170
I believe that's Itomi-san from Renpu.

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:40.050
<b>President's Office</b>

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:40.050
What do you mean, they were 
protected by jurisdiction?

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.930
I am sorry.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.410
Determining the enemy's location, 
carrying out a sneak attack,

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:50.110
and then slinking back after 
failing to destroy them.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:54.020
Seems that I overestimated you.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:57.840
I have no interest in foolish tournaments,

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:03.530
but your worth is measured by getting 
a 100% success rate on your missions.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.920
Perhaps I have been a bit too overprotective.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:11.520
It is open.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:14.460
What do you want?

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:17.760
Yukari-sama ordered me to bring you.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.740
Yukari-sama did?

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:22.640
Renpu President.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.550
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.830
I do not remember giving you 
permission to pursue them.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.970
W-We ascertained the 
location of the traitors,

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:33.610
and I thought they might get away, 
so I made the decision myself.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.690
I will not permit unauthorized actions.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:39.190
B-But I cannot forgive them!

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:41.600
The traitors who turned their okatana on you

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:44.480
are running around freely, 
right within our reach!

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:47.290
Why will you not allow me to go after them?!

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:50.820
President Takatsu,
 you have said quite enough.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:52.000
Damn you.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:53.270
Yukina...

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:54.250
Y-Yes!

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:57.250
Do what you need to do first.

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:58.970
Yukari-sama...

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.210
That's enough. You're dismissed.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:11.290
Yomi...

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.160
Stretch!

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.090
Are you all set?

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.490
Yeah.

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:29.700
Well then, mission start!

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.170
Found you!

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:50.430
You're Minoseki Academy second-year
 middle school student Etou Kanami, correct?

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.560
That's right.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:58.320
I am Kohagura Ellen, first-year high 
school student at Osafune Girls' School.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:02.510
And this is Kaoru.

00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:09.990
Prepare to fight, scoundrel, for turning 
your blade on the head of the Origami family!

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:14.060
By the way, where's Juujou Hiyori?

00:10:14.490 --> 00:10:16.530
Hiyori-chan isn't here,

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:20.110
but if you're after her, I'll deal with you.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:21.970
That will make things easy.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:26.390
What a pain in the butt.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.390
<i>Yakumaru Jigen style?</i>

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.100
What was that?

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.940
<i>Such power...</i>

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.910
I missed. What a pain.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:44.150
If I'd hit you, you would've been smashed.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:47.570
<i>Kongoshi?</i>

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:57.360
Taisha style and martial arts using kongoshi?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.390
<i>I can't just keep my distance 
if I'm going to face her.</i>

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.260
<i>I have to get closer!</i>

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:12.850
<i>I can't get any closer like this!</i>

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:15.600
<i>These two, it's like they're 
two working as one!</i>

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.350
<i>Darn it!</i>

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.100
Yes, I caught you!

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:19.440
Now, Kaoru!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.360
That was close.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:29.280
Hiyori-chan? Why?

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:31.070
Why aren't <i>you</i> running away?

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:31.950
But...

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.330
Now it's finally two-on-two.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:46.700
It's no use,
 they're completely working as one.

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:53.560
That's because Kaoru and 
I are the best partners!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.970
Well, then...

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:02.360
<i>If I turn the impact back around on her...</i>

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.530
What? An aradama?

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.530
That's right. You have good eyes.

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:14.160
What's going on?!

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.250
I lost in our match the other day.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.740
I wonder how today's will turn out.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.300
You're going to fight like this?

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:32.800
I'd get in trouble if I fought 
like this in a match.

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:38.850
En garde!

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:59.040
So our assassins are from Osafune this time?

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:01.290
How did you know where we were?

00:13:02.870 --> 00:13:04.890
That is a secret.

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:09.300
What? An aradama?

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:11.930
It apparently obeys her.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:14.130
So you're using an aradama?

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.810
Answer the question. Otherwise...

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:19.110
Hiyori-chan!

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:23.050
I will complete my objective 
and kill anyone who tries to stop me.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:25.170
Please wait a minute.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.900
Feel like talking now?

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:30.820
Um... in a bit, after about five seconds.

00:13:30.820 --> 00:13:32.280
Five seconds?

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.160
That's...

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.870
S Equipment.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:45.010
Used for completely annihilating aradama.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:49.460
I've only ever heard about the 
S Equipment once before, in class.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:50.550
Same here.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.610
Changing complete.

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:57.050
Meet armored Kaoru.

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:01.560
Our situation has reversed now.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:03.120
Hiyori-chan...

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.020
Right.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:06.520
Ready, let's go!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:10.190
What? Huh? Huh?

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:14.400
Hey! This is the star mecha's big scene!

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:22.530
All those from Renpu are being withdrawn. 
We are backing out from this case.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.320
I was of no use at all.

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:29.300
What's wrong?

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.620
We have an inquiry from Yokosuka Base

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:35.470
asking whether or not we dispatched 
S equipment to the south.

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.510
S Equipment?

00:14:37.510 --> 00:14:40.270
We have not received any such report.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.140
Here is the image.

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:47.820
Those do look like the launching containers.

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:49.770
Our withdrawal is postponed!

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:52.780
Find out exactly where those landed!

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.860
Shidou-san, Konohana-san,

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:01.120
your dispatch orders from 
Yukari-sama have come.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.500
Please get ready.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:09.290
They're not coming after us.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:12.850
The equipment is still in development.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:15.510
So it should only be usable for 
a limited amount of time.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:20.060
It's raining again.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:22.570
Looks like it's going to come down.

00:15:29.190 --> 00:15:32.020
For Yukari-sama to let us go now...

00:15:32.020 --> 00:15:35.150
This must be important to her.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:39.100
It's unusual for you to 
leave Yukari-sama's side.

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:42.620
My abilities will be useful 
in searching for the enemy.

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:44.870
Will Yume be remaining behind?

00:15:44.870 --> 00:15:48.560
Needless blood would be spilled 
if she were sent along.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:52.790
Ah, I'm so bored I'm gonna die.

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:54.250
That's true.

00:15:54.610 --> 00:15:57.310
But it is unlikely

00:15:57.710 --> 00:16:01.290
that S Equipment would exist outside the 
Origami family's jurisdiction.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:04.190
There aren't any other organizations 
beyond the Origami family

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.850
or the Administration who 
can develop that equipment.

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:09.270
If there was, that would 
mean the Administration is...

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:12.190
We would have to use that plan.

00:16:12.630 --> 00:16:16.880
If there actually is a rebel faction in 
the special military, as the rumors say,

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:18.190
then it's not so unlikely.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:24.200
Yukari-sama is trying to ascertain 
if they have contacted those girls.

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:27.100
Or perhaps that's already the case.

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:35.500
So, how did they do?

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:38.540
Ability-wise, they were fine.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.470
Other than that...

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:43.090
What did you think, Kaoru?

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:46.540
Seems like they weren't just being reckless.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:59.020
Thank you for coming to help me.

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:07.390
When I faced off with you earlier, 
I thought about something.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:11.200
Your sword is heavy.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.900
When it comes to killing people,
 I believe that the girl from last night,

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:18.750
Sayaka-chan, is superior.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:22.620
And as far as power goes, the girl with 
the oodachi earlier is better as well.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:27.310
But your sword is the heaviest.

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:29.410
What are you trying to say?

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.610
I realized that your sword is 
weighed down with your will.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:39.930
Achieving an objective takes a 
strong will. That's why it's heavy.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:46.710
That time, in the final 
match of the tournament,

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:51.470
I could only think of how 
you were going to attack me.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:54.540
My mind was only stuck on you,

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:59.210
but you never really did see me, did you?

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:04.070
I was pretty upset about that.

00:18:04.070 --> 00:18:05.470
You were?

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:08.970
Yeah, since you ignored me.

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:17.560
Later, if I'd just stayed back and watched,
 they would've killed you.

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:24.560
It's like you said. I wasn't prepared,

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:26.480
nor did I have any particular intention.

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:29.250
But now I can say that I do.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:32.850
If my sword is one that protects,

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:36.620
then I will protect you and your objective.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:40.580
Then that would just be 
aiding in someone's murder.

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:41.710
It won't.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:44.750
You will kill the head of the family...

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:48.690
No, an aradama pretending to be human.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.010
I won't allow you to kill anyone else.

00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:53.570
That's my resolution.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.730
The reason I want to 
defeat Origami Yukari...

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:06.350
You told me I could talk about 
it if I ever felt like it, right?

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:07.520
I'll tell you now.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:09.450
Okay.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:13.870
Kanami, you know about the 
great aradama incident

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:16.110
that happened twenty years ago, don't you?

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:19.100
The Great Disaster of Sagami Bay?

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:23.590
The worst aradama ever in history, 
which appeared in Enoshima,

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:27.190
and was vanquished by Origami Yukari-sama, 
the current presidents of the Five Schools,

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:29.200
and the Special Religious Military Units?

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:36.060
Yes, and my mother was part of a Special 
Religious Military Unit at that time.

00:19:37.580 --> 00:19:39.790
No records of her remain.

00:19:39.790 --> 00:19:43.190
Not surprising, considering 
everything is a matter of doctrine

00:19:43.190 --> 00:19:45.770
since the incident is 
well-known around the world.

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:47.740
What do you mean?

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:52.930
The truth of it all is 
written in this letter.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:56.110
It talks about what you saw,

00:19:56.700 --> 00:20:00.960
the true identity of Origami Yukari, and...

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:06.110
the great aradama that was 
said to have been vanquished.

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:12.970
The worst thing to have threatened the 
existence of this country, no, the world,

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:17.210
lives even now, wreaking havoc.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:19.390
That's what she is.

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:22.820
And the only one among the gathered Toji

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:26.450
who possessed the power to 
destroy it was my mother.

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:30.360
Your mother?

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:33.520
But she couldn't completely destroy it.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.310
It became a part of
 Origami Yukari and survived.

00:20:39.470 --> 00:20:42.160
After exhausting her Toji powers,

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.620
I watched my mother waste 
away over the years.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:49.570
And last year, she drew her last 
breath as I watched over her.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:53.390
That night, I made a vow.

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:58.710
I would destroy the thing 
that stole my mother's life

00:20:58.710 --> 00:21:03.500
and even now continues to sneak 
around in the human world.

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:07.470
I would finish the task 
my mother left undone.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:17.250
Part of the heaviness you 
mentioned is my duty as a Toji,

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:19.850
but the other half is my own personal grudge.

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:22.970
That is why you do not need to accompany me.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:26.030
You're right.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:36.010
It seems pretty heavy, though, 
so I'll take on half of it.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:52.400
Perfect timing. The rain has stopped.

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.010
Now, then, to the mountain hunt.

00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:39.890
<b>Next Episode  A Night of Mountain Hunting</b>
